  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 210 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nAfter a brief cool down and some rainfall across portions of our \nregion, warmer and drier conditions return at the start of a new \nwork week. The upper trough that initially brought us a cold \nfront over the weekend slides eastward. In its place, upper \nridging centered over the Desert Southwest begins to build toward \nour region, prompting warmer temperatures. Triple digit highs \nreturn to much of the Permian Basin, SE NM, the Upper Trans Pecos,\nand the Rio Grande Valley Monday and Tuesday. Midweek, the ridge \nlooks to become slightly flattened by an upper trough translating \nacross the northern US. Lower heights allow temperatures to drop \nback a couple of degrees. Temperatures Wednesday through Friday \nare forecast to reach the upper 90s to low 100s each afternoon, \nwith the hottest conditions generally near and along the river \nvalleys. Overnight lows can be expected to cool mainly into the \n70s each night. Aside from isolated afternoon convection in the \nvicinity of the higher elevations, most look to remain dry through\nthe Long Term period.",
